      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 1700s, Isleños—Canary Islanders recruited by Spanish governor Bernardo de Gálvez—settled Poydras to boost agriculture and defense.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/poydras_louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Poydras suffered severe flooding and infrastructure loss when Hurricane Katrina struck on August 29, 2005.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poydras%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Poydras sits on the east bank of the Mississippi, just upriver from the Plaquemines Parish line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
